// A line-calculator interpreter as a realistic two-package `rene build`:
// the app package carries a lexer, a recursive-descent parser, and an
// evaluator split across modules (`mod lexer/parser/eval`, `root::`/bare
// package paths across files), and every byte of console traffic goes
// through the `textio` dependency — a pure polyffi package whose `Text` is
// the runtime's rc string held opaquely. The interpreter itself exercises
// the data-structure pipeline end to end: token cons-lists, an AST, an
// association-list environment threaded through persistent `let` bindings,
// and per-line error recovery (parse errors, division by zero, unbound
// variables) that resynchronizes at the next newline.

// RUN: %rene build --manifest-path %S/calc/rene.ncl --build-dir %t.bdir %rrc_linker | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LISTING

// LISTING: {{[/\\]}}dev{{[/\\]}}calc

// RUN: %t.bdir/dev/calc%exe_ext < %S/calc/example.in | %FileCheck %s

// The session, line by line: two bindings, arithmetic against them, a
// rebinding expression, then one of each error — all reported in input
// order, each recovered at its newline.
// CHECK:      bind 19
// CHECK-NEXT: bind 12
// CHECK-NEXT: = 228
// CHECK-NEXT: = 200
// CHECK-NEXT: bind 235
// CHECK-NEXT: = 35
// CHECK-NEXT: division by zero
// CHECK-NEXT: parse error
// CHECK-NEXT: unbound variable
// CHECK-NEXT: = -220

// The release profile (aggressive optimization, and a two-unit link from
// the manifest's `codegen_units`) is the same interpreter: identical
// session transcript from the identical input.
// RUN: %rene build --manifest-path %S/calc/rene.ncl --build-dir %t.bdir --profile release %rrc_linker | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RELEASE
// RUN: %t.bdir/release/calc%exe_ext < %S/calc/example.in | %FileCheck %s

// RELEASE: {{[/\\]}}release{{[/\\]}}calc
